## Finding

**File:** `SnoopWPF.Agent.Engine/LocatorResolver.cs:270-285`

\`\`\`csharp
private static bool MatchesPath(WpfLocator locator, TreeItem item)
{
    var segments = locator.Value.Split(new[] { '\\\\' }, ...);
    var lastSegment = segments[segments.Length - 1];
    return string.Equals(shortName, lastSegment, ...);   // ← only the LAST segment
}
\`\`\`

`path=Window\\Grid\\StackPanel\\Button` is semantically equivalent to `type=Button`. `path=DialogA\\Button` and `path=DialogB\\Button` match identically. Silent wrong-element targeting in multi-window scenarios.

## Fix

Walk all segments bottom-up. For segment N (leaf), match `item`. For segment N-1, match `item.Parent`. Etc. All must match for the locator to resolve.

\`\`\`csharp
TreeItem? cursor = item;
for (int i = segments.Length - 1; i >= 0; i--)
{
    if (cursor == null) return false;
    if (!SegmentMatches(segments[i], cursor)) return false;
    cursor = cursor.Parent;
}
return true;
\`\`\`

## Acceptance

- Test: `path=WindowA\\Button` does NOT match a Button inside WindowB.
- Existing tests for leaf-only match still pass with updated assertions.
- Build + suite clean.

## Scope

- `SnoopWPF.Agent.Engine/LocatorResolver.cs`
- `SnoopWPF.Agent.Tests/LocatorResolutionTests.cs` (add path-hierarchy tests)
